Z||000003||theogre||11-02-1999||05:06 PM||||It's not ECM controlled.<P>Allot of things moved in 87. If I have all these right.......<P>the one in the thermostat is the ECM sensor. the one on the corner of the head is the light/gauge one.<P>the one for the fan is burried in 87. As yet I don't see where. It's raining out so I can't dig for it now. It's small. it's either near the oil pressure sender, or hiding under the scatter guard on the exhaust side. I see a green wire heading under the intake, but I can't confirm it.<P>You can confirm the one on the corner of the head by simply grounding each terminal. either the fan will come on, the light will come on or gauge will move.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-02-1999).]||||reg||1
